      "description": "South Park Street Cemetery is located on Mother Teresa Sarani of Kolkata. Opened in 1767, the cemetery is one of the earliest non-church cemeteries in the world, which was opened to relieve the pressure on other burial grounds in Central Kolkata. Most of the graves are tall and imposing, a mix of Gothic and Indo-Saracenic styles. The cemetery was in use until 1790 and is now a heritage site, protected by the Archaeological Survey of India.",
